    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302-a1">

                <pb facs="0346" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg270"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Ambassador Sharp
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 8, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: With reference to a note from
                    the Embassy dated the 17th of this [sic] month, I have the honor to inform you
                    that the French recruiting authorities have never been aware that Adrien J.
                    Kirghis had acquired a foreign nationality.</p>
                <p>Under these circumstances, the aforementioned, being born in France of parents
                    who themselves were born in France, is considered to be a Frenchman and is at
                    present about to be called to the colors.</p>
                <p>With assurances [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jules Cambon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
